(1)    1600 :                    /// @param md_x multiplicand, below 1024
(1)    1600 :                    /// @param AC multiplier
(1)    1600 :                    /// @return AC quotient, which must fit in 12 bits
(1)    1600 :                    /// @clobber MQ L
(1)    1600 :                    /// The multiply shifts the product right into MQ as the multiplier
(1)    1600 :                    /// leaves it, one octal digit of the multiplier per pass. The high
(1)    1600 :                    /// word, held in AC, stays below 2*multiplicand; taking out 2*F while
(1)    1600 :                    /// it can leaves a remainder below F to start the divide, and puts
(1)    1600 :                    /// those quotient bits at the bottom of MQ. The divide then shifts the
(1)    1600 :                    /// product's low bits back out of MQ while quotient bits enter at the
(1)    1600 :                    /// bottom, in as many passes. Its remainder may go negative instead of
(1)    1600 :                    /// being restored.
